WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.633
Embeddings.

2
00:00:01.933 --> 00:00:08.700
Half of this volume runs on one idea: turning text into a point, so that similar meaning lands close together.

3
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.300
An embedding model maps text to a vector.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.500
The key property: similar meaning becomes geometric closeness.

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.300
That single property powers retrieval, clustering, deduplication, and semantic caching.

6
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.233
Picture each text as a point.

7
00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:28.100
Solar flare disrupted comms lands here.

8
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.000
And a CME hitting the magnetosphere lands right next to it.

9
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.100
Asteroid flyby lands far away, close to its own neighbor.

10
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.900
That geometry is retrieval.

11
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.700
Compare every pair, and you get a block pattern.

12
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.633
The two sun texts score about zero point seven.

13
00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:46.667
So do the two asteroid texts.

14
00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:49.767
Across the groups, only about zero point two.

15
00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.967
Here it is with sentence transformers.

16
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.867
We load one embedding model.

17
00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:59.345
We encode the texts, normalized, and multiply by the transpose.

18
00:00:59.345 --> 00:01:01.533
That gives the similarity matrix.

19
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:03.358
Two traps.

20
00:01:03.358 --> 00:01:09.100
If you mix models or versions between documents and queries, you compare garbage to garbage.

21
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.925
And your model choice caps the whole system.

22
00:01:11.925 --> 00:01:14.967
Check the leaderboard, but decide on your own corpus.

23
00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.367
A real fix from Mission Control RAG.

24
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:25.800
A general model put solar array degradation, a power issue, nearly on top of solar activity, space weather.

25
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.767
The team swapped to a stronger model and re-indexed.

26
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:33.012
The clusters separated, and wrong-document retrievals vanished.

27
00:01:33.012 --> 00:01:34.702
Nothing downstream changed.

28
00:01:34.702 --> 00:01:35.767
The geometry did.

29
00:01:36.967 --> 00:01:37.719
Let's recap.

30
00:01:37.719 --> 00:01:40.100
Embeddings turn meaning into position.

31
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.300
Similar text lands close together.

32
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.367
Queries and documents must share the same model.

33
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:48.171
And your model choice caps RAG quality.

34
00:01:48.171 --> 00:01:50.033
Next up: chunking strategies.
